WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.170
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Hi.

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.190
My name is Ryan.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.920
And I'd like to show you around
the Google Cloud Console, where

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.170
you can manage your Google
Cloud resources directly

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.580
from the web.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.460
In the next few minutes, we'll
explore several key areas

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.440
of the console that can
help you as you begin

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.300
your journey with Google Cloud.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.020
Ready?

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.950
Let's get started.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.184
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.590
Google Cloud resources are the
fundamental components that

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.990
make up Google Cloud Services.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.290
These may include Compute Engine
virtual machines, Cloud Storage

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.610
buckets, Cloud SQL database
instances, and more.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.350
Resources are organized
hierarchically

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.510
using projects and folders.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.060
Projects are how you group
resources together and are

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.430
the first level
of the hierarchy.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:47.610
All resources must belong
to exactly one project.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.980
So a given Compute
Engine virtual machine

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.730
or a Cloud Storage bucket
would belong to one project.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.880
Optionally, projects can
belong to organizations,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.590
which provide
centralized visibility

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.500
and control across all
projects in a given org.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.990
An organization helps
administrators for your company

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.890
or group manage billing or
security across many projects.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.560
You can further organize your
company's departments or teams

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.730
into folders.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.710
Folders can contain
projects, and also

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.190
subfolders for further
structure and nesting.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.490
When you open
console.cloud.google.com,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.860
here's the landing
page dashboard.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.500
At the top, you can see
which Google Cloud project

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.043
you're currently viewing.

00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:28.710
You can click the
project name to switch

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.360
to a different project.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.520
If you do so, you'll
see the resources

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.170
for your other project.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.990
You can also create a
new project right here.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.110
Another key area of the console
is the left navigation menu,

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.670
located in the top-left corner.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:46.290
This menu helps you access
your Google Cloud Services.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.410
For example, if you navigate
to the Cloud Storage section,

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:52.530
you can create new Cloud
Storage buckets, upload objects,

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.505
and download objects.

00:01:54.505 --> 00:01:56.130
You can also pin your
favorite products

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.320
to the top for easy access.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.990
I'll pin Storage to make sure
I can quickly get to my buckets

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.790
next time.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.920
Next up, we have the
search bar, which

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.560
allows you to quickly search
for Google Cloud products,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.199
resources, and documentation.

00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:12.120
For example, you could
search for the name

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.420
of one of your other projects
if you want to switch to it.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.220
If you search for
Cloud Run, you'll

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.950
see links to the Cloud Run
section of the Console,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.010
documentation and tutorials
related to Cloud Run,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.530
and a list of Cloud
Run-related APIs that you

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.540
might want to manage.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.180
The home dashboard provides
a high-level overview

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.460
of your Google Cloud
project, giving you

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.890
information about
key metrics, billing,

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.020
and getting started guides.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.210
The dashboard is
customizable, allowing

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:42.070
you to show, hide, and
reorder the different cards

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.700
how you want.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.410
There's also the
Activity stream,

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.900
which shows you information
about all the activities

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.100
happening across your Google
Cloud resources in one place.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.260
For example, you can
see which projects

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.050
have been updated, what
your teammates are doing,

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:00.650
or audit access to your
Google Cloud resources.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.020
Next is the APIs and
Services section,

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:06.470
where you can do things
like enable or disable APIs,

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.580
view API usage information,
and manage credentials.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.610
If you click Enable APIs
and Services at the top,

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.927
you'll be brought
to the API Library.

00:03:15.927 --> 00:03:17.510
This is where you
can view information

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.630
about the hundreds of different
Google Cloud APIs across areas

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.260
like Maps, Machine Learning,
Google Workspace, and more.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.290
If you click on
Cloud Vision API,

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.080
you'll be brought to the Cloud
Vision API page, where you can

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.545
click Enable to enable the API.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.920
This allows you
to use the Vision

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.140
API in your applications.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.570
If you ever get stuck,
the Support section

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.080
is also accessible right
from the navigation menu.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.720
You can get help via
chat, over the phone,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.075
or from other community members.

00:03:47.075 --> 00:03:48.950
There are several
different support offerings

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.110
that you can compare
and contrast to see what

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.390
makes the most sense for you.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.390
Another key part of the console
is Cloud Identity and Access

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.762
Management, or Cloud IAM.

00:03:58.762 --> 00:04:01.220
Here, you can manage and create
permissions for your Google

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.930
Cloud resources.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.150
As your team grows,
you can grant access

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.250
to teammates in Cloud IAM.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.070
You can add users, groups,
or service accounts

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:11.540
and assign them
any number of roles

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.950
to grant them the
permission they need.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.010
For example, you can
add your friend James

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.279
as an editor for your
Google Cloud project.

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:21.920
Next up, we have Cloud
Shell, which provides you

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.170
with command-line access
to your cloud resources

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.360
directly from your web browser.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.150
Powered by a small virtual
machine with persistent disk

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.910
space, it comes pre-installed
with helpful tools

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:35.120
like the Google Cloud
SDK, Docker, git,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.580
and various
programming languages.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.763
This makes it easy to get
started and explore Google

00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:41.930
Cloud without having to
download additional software

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.130
to your local device.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.037
There's also Cloud
Shell Editor, which

00:04:46.037 --> 00:04:47.870
makes it easy for you
to write code directly

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.780
from your web browser and
deploy it to the cloud.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.310
The Billing section
of the console

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.990
is where you can
manage billing accounts

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.000
and link your projects to them.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.710
A Cloud Billing
account defines who

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.860
pays for a given set of
Google Cloud resources.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.810
To use Google
Cloud Services, you

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.860
must have a valid
billing account linked

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.992
to your Google Cloud projects.

00:05:07.992 --> 00:05:10.200
The billing account can be
linked to payment methods,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:14.130
like a free trial, a credit
card, or a bank account.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:16.380
There are also interactive
quick-start experiences

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.210
available in the Console.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.040
These tutorials,
which you can find

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.010
on the home dashboard in
the Getting Started section,

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.170
guide you through how to
accomplish essential tasks

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.450
with different cloud products.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.610
For example, this
tutorial guides you

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.710
through how to create
a Cloud Storage bucket,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.720
upload a file to the bucket,
and delete the bucket.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.670
And you can do this all
in under five minutes.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.310
Beyond the web portal,
the Google Cloud Console

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.920
is also available on
Android and iOS mobile apps.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.610
You can use these to monitor
and manage your Google Cloud

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.100
applications on the go.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.690
So there you have
it, an overview

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.465
of what the Google Cloud Console
is and how you can get started.

00:05:55.465 --> 00:05:57.840
Make sure to check out the
other episodes of Google Cloud

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.940
Essentials, where we
cover the Google Cloud

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:04.210
SDK, the free trial,
key use cases, and more.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.600
I can't wait to see what
you built with Google Cloud.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

